<title>UK: Oliver Ashworth shares make dull debut.</title>
<headline>Oliver Ashworth shares make dull debut.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Manchester-based pipeline distribution company Oliver Ashworth Plc  made a dull debut on Monday on the London Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>The shares were quoted at 132-1/2p by 1410 GMT after having been placed at 135p, raising 6.0 million stg after expenses and valuing the company at 26.3 million stg.</p>
<p>Trading volume in the stock reached 181,487 shares.</p>
<p>The sponsor to the float was NM Rothschild and the broker was Williams de Broe.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
